    <item>
      <title></title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/en/research/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/en/research/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;research&#34;&gt;Research&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I am interested in phenomena of systems composed of non-equilibrium elements. One example is active matter, which consume energy and turns it into propulsion. Another example is granular particles, whose particle sizes are large enough and thus thermal relaxation is negligible.
Currently, I conduct experiments with bacteria and colloidal systems to measure the magnetic response of active matter.
&lt;img class=&#34;research-hero-image&#34; src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/images/research.png&#34; alt=&#34;Research image&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;experimental-techniques-i-have-learned-in-my-study&#34;&gt;Experimental techniques I have learned in my study&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I designed and built experimental setups to apply magnetic fields to active systems and observe their behavior. Through my projects, I developed skills in the following areas.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
